WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.167
-Welcome back to the show.
We love having you here.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.934
And, gosh, I got real
competitive with that game,

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:07.267
and I apologize.
-So did I.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.868
I think it's fair to say
that "Zimmy" won.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.767
Jimmy and Zoey together.
Don't you think?

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.234
-I'll take a win for Zimmy
anytime.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:16.634
-I think --
I think you gave that to me.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.300
-Can I just say how excited
I am that you're here?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.334
Because I'm talking to a star of
the Marvel cinematic universe.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.000
-Are you? [ Laughs ]

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.968
-Yes. Do you know that?

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:28.267
-I -- Well, okay. I was in --

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:32.300
Well, I played
girl in the bathroom

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.033
who got attacked by the lizard
coming out of the toilet

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.300
in "The Amazing Spider-Man."

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.067
I'm sure you guys
all saw me in that, right?

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.901
-Of course. We loved it.
That was our favorite --

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.267
-Yeah, well, maybe there
wasn't an immediate clap

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.667
because I was actually credited
as "Gossip Girl,"

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.634
so maybe that's maybe more of
what you recognized me as.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.167
[ Laughter ]
But I was in one scene.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.734
-Was Andrew Garfield
in it with you?

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.968
-Yes, Andrew Garfield --
No, he wasn't in the scene.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:55.367
-No, of course not.
-No, just...

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.534
-I was just testing you
to see if you remember it.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.400
-I remembered it. Yeah.
I was in one scene.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.501
I had no lines.
I was so excited.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.501
And for whatever reason,
they used that scene

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.501
as the, like, teaser
at Comic-Con.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:09.534
And so people thought
I had a big part

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.968
and kept saying to me like,

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.300
"Oh, my God, you're the star of
'The Amazing Spider-Man.'

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.834
I didn't know
that you're the star

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:17.200
of 'The Amazing Spider-Man.'"
It's like, "I didn't either."

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.000
But I went to the theaters,
and I was cut out of the movie.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.501
So it doesn't really
have a happy ending.

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:23.067
But I think technically,
I'm in the MCU.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.367
I'm, like, in the
black-hole part of the MCU.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.868
-Yeah, you were cut out
of the film, unfortunately,

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.868
so no one got to see it.
-I have not seen it.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:33.467
-But I have friends
in high places.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.667
[ laughter ]
I got the clip.

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.133
-I actually really
haven't seen this,

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.133
so I don't know how you...
-Actually -- No, really.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.901
We have the clip.
I'm gonna show it to you.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.501
Also, I want to have
the camera on you

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.100
'cause I want
to see your reaction.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.601
I will say the visual effects
are not quite there

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.501
because it actually
was cut out of the film.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.434
But this is Zoey Deutch
in "The Amazing Spider-Man."

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.667
Let's take a look at this.
The debut.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:58.634
♪♪

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.367
-Oh, my gosh.
-There you go.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.834
♪♪

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.501
-Wow.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.067
♪♪

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.834
Oh, my God. Yikes.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:18.367
♪♪

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:19.934
[ Both scream ]

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:24.534
-Wow. That is unbelievable.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.634
-Really?
-Yeah, I loved it.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.534
-It feels like --
Wow. That was interesting.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:29.868
-I loved it.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.934
-CGI has gotten a lot better
in the last ten years.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:35.467
And I hope my acting, too.
That was...

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.701
"Aah!" Horrifying.

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.334
-You've been acting
for over a decade.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:41.667
Did you always know
you wanted to be an actor?

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.000
-I think so. But -- I think so.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.300
Yeah, I've always
been loud and annoying.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.634
But I accidentally found

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.467
the exact moment, I think,
that I claimed

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.801
that this was my path
that I wanted to go down.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.100
There was an interview
20 years ago with my mom,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.534
who's also an actress,
and the interviewer asked her

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.968
if she thinks her kids
want to be actors one day.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.400
And so I brought the video
for you. There you go.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.100
-I appreciate that.
Your mom is the one and only

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.067
Lea Thompson, by the way,
who is amazing.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.334
[ Applause ]

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.067
This is...

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.734
This is Lea Thompson
being interviewed 20 years ago.

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:15.133
Take a look at this.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.968
-So, Lea, does either daughter
have any interest

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.400
in acting or anything so far?

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.601
-I want to.
I really want to be an actress.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:22.367
-Oh, well, that's the first time
I've heard of that.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.334
Oh, you want to be an actress?
-Yeah.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.434
-'Cause you see
how glamorous it is?

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.267
-No!
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.100
-Well, that's part of it.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.267
-Yeah. Oh. Come on!

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:34.968
-That is part of it.

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:37.601
-Oh, my gosh.
How cute is that? Come on.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:40.234
It's only part of it.
So charming.

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:41.934
Your new movie --

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.534
"Not Okay," by the way,
is the name of the movie.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.067
-Are you okay?
-I'm okay.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.534
-You guys okay?
-Yeah, we're okay.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:47.767
-Everyone's okay?

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:50.634
-But in this movie,
your character tells a lie

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.834
that gets out of hand.

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.100
Are you a good liar
in real life?

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.434
-I don't know. Am I?

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:57.968
No, I'm a good liar.

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:01.367
But then I have to immediately
confess like I just did.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:04.100
And I did in the video, too.
I say like, "No!"

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.968
-You can't help.
-I can't help it.

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:07.434
-But you're good at --

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.934
I heard you're good at telling
if someone is telling a lie.

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.234
-My sister says that
I'm a human lie detector.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.934
But I don't know.
I don't know.

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.901
-I want to challenge you
to maybe a game of

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.968
"Two Truths and a Lie"
if that's okay with you.

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.434
-Okay.
-Alright?

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.367
-On your card here is two truths
about you and a lie.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.901
I don't know.
And I have mine here.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:26.868
Okay. I have here.
So maybe you read yours first.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.767
Two of these are true
and one is a lie.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.767
And I'm gonna see
if I can guess yours.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.367
-[ Clears throat ]

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:36.000
In a span of two years...
-That's a lie.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.501
-...I got stuck in three
different elevators.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:42.133
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.501
I took -- Do you want to ask me
questions, or shall I continue?

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:47.267
-Do I ask questions?
-I don't know. If you want to.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.601
-Huh. I think
you're being too forward.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:52.667
I think it's true.
-Okay.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:55.734
I took my pet beetle with me
to school for a month.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.000
-A pet beetle?

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.300
-Beetle Fren.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.467
-What's his name?
-Beetle Fren. F-R-E-N.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.734
-Beetle Fren?
-Yeah.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.133
-That makes me believe
that it's true,

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.734
but how could you invent
the name Beetle Fren?

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.667
It's really cute.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.767
Okay. Beetle Fren.
Do you miss Beetle Fren?

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.834
-Well, he was always dead.
-Okay. Alright.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:17.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:19.300
Oh, my gosh.
Your pet was always dead.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.701
Alright.
-It was always dead.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.000
-Okay.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.267
-I once peed my pants
on Robert De Niro's plane.

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:27.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:30.133
-Now, are you sure
this is not my truth?

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.501
[ Laughter ]
-They mixed up the cards?

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:33.834
-Hmm.

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.434
Wow. You peed your pants
on Robert De Niro's plane.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:39.367
I feel like maybe you were
a baby or something,

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:40.567
and you might have done that.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.467
-Why was I on --
Why would I be...

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:45.868
-Well...

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:47.267
Gosh.
What was the first one again?

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:48.467
It was stuck in three elevators?

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:49.734
-In the span of two years,

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:51.901
I got stuck in
three different elevators.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.667
What do you guys think?

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:56.434
-I think the first one is a lie.

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:58.601
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:01.901
-Unfortunately,
you are wrong, Jimmy.

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:04.901
[ Buzzer ]
-Do you get to tell me which --

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:06.400
-Yeah.
-You did stuck in an elevator?

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.133
-No, I didn't take my pet beetle
with me to school for a month.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:11.434
I had a pet beetle,
but I didn't take him to school,

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.067
so I'm sorry.

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:15.400
-That's a -- Come on!
You tricked me.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.367
-Well, that's the game.
I'm supposed to trick you.

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:18.567
-I know. Beetle Fren.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:19.834
How did you -- And old were you

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:21.767
when you peed your pants
on Robert De Niro's plane?

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:23.868
-That was really recently,
unfortunately.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.367
[ Laughter ]
What in the world?

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:28.734
-That was very recently.
-Oh, my God.

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:30.467
Were you just --

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:33.934
-Well, the bathroom didn't work,
and I had to pee.

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.367
I always have to pee.
-Okay.

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:38.234
-I have to now because
we just played a beer game.

00:06:38.234 --> 00:06:40.734
So I don't know what's going
to happen here, folks.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.300
It could be exciting content
for tonight.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.267
[ Laughter ] Anyway...

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:46.334
-Should I read
my two truths and a lie

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:47.367
and see if you can tell?

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:49.200
-Please.
-Okay.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.234
I'm going to run through these.
Ready?

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.067
-Okay. No questions.
Okay. Got it.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:53.400
-I stole something from the set

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.734
of the "Seinfeld" series finale.

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:01.801
When Big Bird was on the show,
a feather fell off of him,

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:03.133
and I kept the feather
and taped it

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:05.000
to the bottom of this desk.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.734
-That's true.

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:07.801
That's true.
-You think it's true?

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:09.234
-I think that's true.

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:12.000
-I got locked in a bathroom
on a boat at a Pitbull party.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.534
Justin Timberlake rescued me.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:19.067
-Well, I've also gotten trapped
in a bathroom on a boat.

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:22.234
Not Pitbull's boat, but -- Hmm.

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:24.701
-It feels like
you're trying to trick me

00:07:24.701 --> 00:07:26.567
with the Timber-- Oh, gosh.

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:28.834
It's one or three.
It's one or three.

00:07:28.834 --> 00:07:30.067
Oh, gosh.

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:32.434
What was the thing
that you stole from the set?

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:35.667
What was the thing
that you stole from the set?

00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:37.234
Oh, now you're trying
to trick me.

00:07:37.234 --> 00:07:38.701
You're too good at this.

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.234
You know exactly
what you're doing.

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:41.501
-I don't remember.
It was years ago.

00:07:41.501 --> 00:07:44.400
-You're a liar.
You know exactly what you took.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.934
Tell me, Jimmy.
What did you take?

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:49.133
-I took a -- You would think
it would be, like,

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:51.501
cereal or something, but no.

00:07:51.501 --> 00:07:54.767
I took a toothbrush.

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:56.934
-For some reason, it's so bad

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.067
so that I feel like that one
must be true,

00:07:59.067 --> 00:08:01.834
and I feel like this one
is the lie,

00:08:01.834 --> 00:08:04.834
because you're friends with him,
and it's a -- Uh-oh.

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:06.167
-You're really good.
You're correct.

00:08:06.167 --> 00:08:08.701
Yes, I was never locked
in a bathroom ever.

00:08:08.701 --> 00:08:11.133
[ Dinging ]
You got it.

00:08:11.133 --> 00:08:12.367
-Okay.
-How did you --

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:13.934
You are very good.
-Oh, okay.

00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:16.434
-I snuck into the "Seinfeld"
finale and I stole a toothbrush.

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:17.701
-I found one thing I'm good at.

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:19.834
-Wow. No, you're good
at a lot of things.

00:08:19.834 --> 00:08:22.701
Musical Beers? Hello.
-Well...

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:25.100
-Can we tell everyone
what "Not Okay" is about?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.868
-Yes.
"Not Okay" is about --

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:29.000
It's a satire about a girl
named Danni Sanders

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.400
who fakes a trip
on Instagram to Paris

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.901
to impress her co-worker.

00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:36.267
And while she's allegedly there,
a terrorist attack happens,

00:08:36.267 --> 00:08:38.334
and she lies
and says that she survives it.

00:08:38.334 --> 00:08:42.501
And the unraveling of the lie
and her finding out the hard way

00:08:42.501 --> 00:08:44.801
that the Internet
loves a takedown.

00:08:44.801 --> 00:08:45.934
That's what it's about.

00:08:45.934 --> 00:08:47.467
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:49.701
Here's Zoey Deutch
in "Not Okay."

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:50.801
Take a look at this.

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:52.501
♪♪
-Hey, mom.

00:08:52.501 --> 00:08:53.834
Guess what.

00:08:53.834 --> 00:08:57.734
I got invited to a writers'
retreat in Paris.

00:08:57.734 --> 00:08:59.934
Yes, really.

00:08:59.934 --> 00:09:02.601
No, it's not a scam.

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:05.000
It has a website.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.334
Hey, guys. Crazy plot twist.

00:09:07.334 --> 00:09:08.634
I got an e-mail today

00:09:08.634 --> 00:09:10.968
inviting me to go on
this retreat in Paris.

00:09:10.968 --> 00:09:13.567
I'm on my way to the airport.

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:17.634
♪♪

00:09:17.634 --> 00:09:19.167
-Start with mascara.

00:09:19.167 --> 00:09:21.100
We're gonna be
taking this concealer.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.534
We're going go dot, dot, dot.

00:09:23.534 --> 00:09:30.133
♪♪

00:09:30.133 --> 00:09:36.734
♪♪

00:09:36.734 --> 00:09:40.434
-Ah! Zoey Deutch, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:42.434
I just want to show you.

00:09:42.434 --> 00:09:45.100
-We're getting the --
There it is!

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.901
-"Not Okay"
is streaming now on Hulu.

00:09:47.901 --> 00:09:50.400
We'll be right back with a
performance from Saucy Santana.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.467
Stick around, everybody.

